# Keep the build context small and, more importantly, keep secrets out of the image.
#
# .env is the one that matters: it holds the Mongo password, the JWT secret and the WhatsApp
# gateway key. On Render those come from the dashboard's environment variables, never from a
# file baked into a layer that anyone who can pull the image could read back.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

node_modules
npm-debug.log*
.git
.gitignore
.vscode
.idea

uploads
tmp
*.log

# Local one-off scripts and dumps that have no business in a deployed image.
*.mjs.local
dump/
